Two-gross circuit-distance witnesses

The circuit construction in gen_bb_memory.py and the circuit transcription
and Pauli propagation in verify_transcription.py are adapted from
decoder_setup.py in Sergey Bravyi's BivariateBicycleCodes repository:

https://github.com/sbravyi/BivariateBicycleCodes
Commit: fa77e3333d3ec44c79d8f914dd24c040d1da471b
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0 (included in LICENSE).

The accompanying paper is:
Sergey Bravyi, Andrew W. Cross, Jay M. Gambetta, Dmitri Maslov,
Patrick Rall, and Theodore J. Yoder,
"High-threshold and low-overhead fault-tolerant quantum memory,"
Nature 627, 778–782 (2024), arXiv:2308.07915.

Adaptations include a Stim circuit generator, explicit noise and boundary
handling, the two-gross and A2/A3-swap parameters, and standalone witness
replay with a binary-rank test of the final logical error. These files are
adaptations, not unmodified copies of the upstream implementation.
